{
  "about": "What is held in each vestige's block of amber (Amber Temple Look Plan §3.2, AmberGlow, `make vestige_shapes`). Each entry is keyed by the vestige's id (its prop `sarc_<id>` without the prefix). `layers` are game-icons.net silhouettes (art/sourced/game_icons, CC BY 3.0, artists credited on the Credits screen) composed into one white-on-transparent texture, art/textures/amber/shapes/<id>.png (`plane: orbit` layers go in <id>_orbit.png, which turns slowly in the block): {icon: \"artist/name\", at: [x, y] (the middle of the silhouette, 0 to 1 over the picture), size (its longer side, 0 to 1), rot (degrees), flip, mode: \"cut\" (a hole in what is under it, a mouth in a face)}. `tint` is the colour the shape is drawn in, dark, inside the amber (a palette colour); `core` and `edge` recolour the block's glass and its light (palette colours, the honey and the ember by default); `touch` is the block's own touch (shaders/world/amber_shape.gdshader and AmberGlow): flecks, bubbles, twitch, cracks, glints, stars_down, fade, sparks_up, ring, orbit, void; `locked` stops the block's light breathing; `cloud` and `cloud_tint` murk the glass, `alpha` how dense it is. A vestige with no `layers` holds no shape.",
